{title: Key of the House of David}
{subtitle: Isaiah 22:20–25; 2 Kings 18:18–37; Isaiah 36:3–22; 2 Kings 19:1–5; Revelation 3:7}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Ab] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On that [Eb]day I will summon my [Bb/D]servant Eliakim son of Hilkiah
[Cm7]I will clothe him with [Eb]your robe and fasten your [Bb/D]sash around him
I will [Cm7]hand your authori[Abmaj7]ty over to him
He [Bb]will be a father [Eb]to those who live in [Bb/D]Jerusalem
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm7]I will place the key of [Ab]the house of David on his shoulder
What he o[Bb]pens no one will shut
What he shuts [Eb]no one will [Bb/D]open
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He is like [Cm7]a peg [Ab]in a firm place
A throne of [Bb]honor for his father's house
[Eb]The glory of the [Bb/D]offspring hangs upon him
The [Cm7]small vessels and the jars are his
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When [Ab]the Assyrian comman[Bb]der came with threats
Eliakim [Eb]asked him to speak in Aramaic
So the people on [Bb/D]the wall would not hear the [Cm7]fear
But the Rabshakeh stood and called out loudly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Eb]We tore our clothes and [Bb/D]went to seek Isaiah
[Cm7]To hear the word of the Lord of [Ab]hosts
To find the guidance that [Bb]we needed then
[Eb]To stand firm in [Bb/D]the face of [Cm7]the storm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]He is like a peg [Bb]in a firm place
A throne [Eb]of honor [Bb/D]for his fa[Cm7]ther's house
The glory of [Eb]the offspring hangs up[Bb/D]on him
The small vessels and [Cm7]the jars are his
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He is like a [Ab]peg in a firm place
[Bb]A throne of honor for his [Eb]father's house
The glory of the offspring hangs upon [Bb/D]him
The small vessels and the [Cm7]jars are his
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The key of the house of [Ab]David is on his shoulder
[Bb]What he opens no one will [Eb]shut
The glory of the offspring hangs upon [Bb/D]him
The small vessels and the [Cm7]jars are his
{end_of_verse}

